  <div class="post-body">
    <p>For more than 20 years, I have worked inside large-scale enterprise systems across insurance, e-commerce, CDN, and telecom. I still get genuine satisfaction from opening a system and asking: why does this actually work the way it does?</p>

    <p>That question has taken me from re-architecting monoliths into microservices to designing distributed log pipelines that process a terabyte of data a day. At the core, I am a problem solver drawn to mathematics, engineering detail, and the work of turning something complex into something clear and workable.</p>

    <h2>What I work on</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Deep expertise in Enterprise Java, Spring Boot, and microservices architecture</li>
      <li>A proven track record of low-risk legacy-to-microservices migrations</li>
      <li>Experience with high-volume distributed systems and near-real-time data pipelines</li>
      <li>Technical mentoring that helps engineering teams level up, not just ship code</li>
      <li>A generalist's instinct for connecting technical decisions to business outcomes</li>
    </ul>

    <p>I currently help organizations through Think &amp; Solve Different Solutions, a Dubai-based consultancy, accelerate their architectural maturity and cloud-readiness. I am also working toward AWS Certified Solutions Architect - Associate, iSAQB CPSA-F, and PSM I.</p>

    <p>This blog is a place to keep notes on the systems, ideas, and questions worth understanding properly.</p>

